{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2449","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2449","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2449\",\"parent_revision\":\"0e43c729fa42dd04f543ebbb9f9c19d9392529ee80634db956fe4101324820fe\",\"root_revision\":\"0e43c729fa42dd04f543ebbb9f9c19d9392529ee80634db956fe4101324820fe\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nbacklog_view is designed to detect when a response exceeds the MCP token budget and automatically return the compact summary (skeleton) view instead of the full body \u2014 enabling progressive disclosure where the agent then loads only the sections it needs via targeted section filters. During a session on 2026-05-24, backlog_view(summary=False, section='X') returned 57\u201358KB responses even with a section filter applied. The consuming agent had to resort to workarounds (ctx_batch_execute to parse persisted output files) just to read two field values.\\n\\nTwo possible failure modes need investigation:\\n1. The auto-detection is not triggering \u2014 the tool returns the full body regardless of size\\n2. The auto-detection triggers and returns the skeleton view, but the skeleton itself is too large (the sections_index plus metadata already exceeds the budget for items with many sections)\\n\\nEither mode is a bug. The contract is: agents should never receive a response that overflows their context. The tool is the correct enforcement point.\\n\\n**Observed**: backlog_view returned persisted output files of 57.9KB and 58.4KB on consecutive calls for issue #2437 (a groomed item with ~27 sections).\\n\\n**Expected**: When response size would exceed the token budget, backlog_view returns summary=True skeleton automatically with a hint explaining how to load specific sections.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: backlog_view does not auto-detect token threshold and fall back to progressive disclosure skeleton view** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 work-backlog-item #2437 planning 2026-05-24\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"617a4513643b734675ed998639be669d8ed7a032ae246322d314e6cf85cf5a92\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCPw-A\"}"}